# A backtick-escaped LOCAL is emitted VERBATIM (#1357), so it does not collide with its
# case-differing twin: `zed` emits `zed` and `` `Zed` `` emits `Zed`, which are two distinct C#
# locals. The escape means the same thing in every declaration space — it preserves the spelling —
# and it is the remedy SPY0522's local-arm message points at for the bare pair (collision_local).

def main() -> None:
    zed: int = 6
    `Zed`: int = 7
    print(zed)
    print(`Zed`)
